---
import CabinetPage from '../layouts/CabinetPage.astro';

const siteUrl = (Astro.site ?? new URL('https://ecommarketdata.com')).origin;
const updated = '5 November 2026';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${siteUrl}/policy/#webpage`,
    name: 'Policies — ecommarketdata',
    url: `${siteUrl}/policy/`,
    dateModified: '2026-11-05',
    inLanguage: 'en-US',
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      '@id': `${siteUrl}/#organization`,
      name: 'ecommarketdata',
      url: `${siteUrl}/`,
      email: 'admin@ecommarketdata.com',
      description:
        'Data extraction, AI agents and software engineering for e-commerce teams.',
    },
  },
];

const contents = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Privacy' },
  { id: 'data-sourcing', label: 'Data sourcing and crawling' },
  { id: 'ai-systems', label: 'AI systems and oversight' },
  { id: 'client-work', label: 'Client work and IP' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'terms', label: 'Terms of use' },
  { id: 'licensing', label: 'Licensing and corrections' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security and retention' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<CabinetPage
  title="Policies — ecommarketdata"
  description="How ecommarketdata handles privacy, crawling, AI systems, client deliverables, licensing and corrections."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
      <h1>Policies</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ecommarketdata is a data engineering and software studio. We build
        extraction systems, AI agents and the software around them. These
        policies explain how we work and what you can expect from us.
      </p>
      <p class="fine-print">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Policy contents">
        <ul>
          {
            contents.map((item) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This page covers this website, our published datasets and our general
          way of working. A signed engagement letter or statement of work takes
          precedence where it differs from what is written here.
        </p>
        <p>
          We work with businesses, not consumers. If you are an individual
          looking for personal data we hold about you, see{' '}
          <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          We collect the minimum needed to run this site and to deliver work. If
          you email us, we keep the message and your reply address so we can
          answer and follow up. For paid engagements we keep business contact
          details, invoices and project records.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal data, and we do not include personal data in
          published datasets. Marketplace figures are reported at market,
          category, listing or seller level — not at the level of an identifiable
          person.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where we process personal data on behalf of a client, we act as a
          processor under their instructions, under a written data processing
          agreement. Where we process data for our own operations, we act as a
          controller and apply the same minimisation rules.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can ask us what we hold about you, request a correction, or ask us
          to delete correspondence at{' '}
          <a href="mailto:admin@ecommarketdata.com">admin@ecommarketdata.com</a>.
          We aim to respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2 id="data-sourcing">Data sourcing and crawling</h2>
        <p>
          Extraction is what we do, so we hold ourselves to a clear standard.
          Our crawlers:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respect <code>robots.txt</code> directives and published rate limits.</li>
          <li>Read only publicly accessible pages unless a client has authorised access in writing.</li>
          <li>Never bypass authentication, paywalls or access controls.</li>
          <li>Identify themselves honestly and provide a contact for site owners.</li>
          <li>Do not collect personal data for resale, profiling or advertising.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Where a platform provides an official API or data feed, we prefer it
          over extraction, and we say so in the engagement. If a site owner asks
          us to stop accessing their pages, we stop.
        </p>
        <p>
          Clients are responsible for confirming that the data they ask us to
          collect may lawfully be collected for their intended use. We will flag
          a request we believe is out of bounds before starting work.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ai-systems">AI systems and oversight</h2>
        <p>
          We build AI agents that read, classify, extract and act on data. Every
          agent we ship runs with bounded permissions: the tools it may call are
          declared, logged and limited to the task.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Agents do not make irreversible changes without an approval step.</li>
          <li>Actions that affect money, customers or live listings require human sign-off.</li>
          <li>Every tool call is logged with its input, output and initiating request.</li>
          <li>Model outputs are treated as suggestions until validated by deterministic checks.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use client data to train third-party foundation models, and
          we do not send confidential material to external services without
          written agreement.
        </p>

        <h2 id="client-work">Client work and IP</h2>
        <p>
          On completion and final payment, clients own the deliverables created
          specifically for them: custom code, pipelines, prompts, documentation
          and the data produced for the engagement.
        </p>
        <p>
          We retain ownership of our pre-existing libraries, internal tooling and
          reusable components. Where those are embedded in a deliverable, the
          client receives a perpetual, non-exclusive licence to use them as part
          of that deliverable.
        </p>
        <p>
          Both sides keep the other's confidential information confidential, and
          we do not name clients publicly without permission.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not set advertising cookies and does not run third-party
          tracking scripts. Essential cookies may be used by our hosting provider
          for security and load balancing. If we add analytics later, this section
          will name the tool, state what it records and explain how to opt out
          before it is enabled.
        </p>

        <h2 id="terms">Terms of use</h2>
        <p>
          Published datasets are provided for research and commercial analysis.
          You may quote figures with attribution to ecommarketdata and a link to
          the dataset page. You may not redistribute the raw dataset, resell it,
          or use it to build a competing data product without a written licence.
        </p>
        <p>
          Figures are best-available estimates unless the page states otherwise.
          They are not audited financial statements and are not investment,
          legal or tax advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not use this site or our services to build a system that breaks
          the law, circumvents access controls, or harms people. We may refuse or
          end an engagement that asks us to do so.
        </p>

        <h2 id="licensing">Licensing and corrections</h2>
        <p>
          Browsing and quoting published data is free with attribution. Custom
          engagements define their own licence in writing: internal use,
          client-facing use, redistribution or commercial embedding.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you believe a figure is wrong, email us with the dataset page and the
          source you are comparing against. Verified corrections are applied and
          noted on the page with the date they changed. We do not silently
          overwrite history.
        </p>

        <h2 id="security">Security and retention</h2>
        <p>
          Access to client systems and data is scoped per person and per project,
          with credentials stored in a secrets manager rather than in code. We
          keep audit logs for changes made by automated systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          We retain project records for as long as needed to support the work and
          meet accounting obligations, then delete or anonymise them. If you need
          a specific retention period, put it in the engagement letter and we will
          follow it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these policies, data requests, crawler access or
          corrections:{' '}
          <a href="mailto:admin@ecommarketdata.com">admin@ecommarketdata.com</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="fine-print">
          This page is a working document and should be reviewed against the legal
          requirements of the jurisdictions you operate in before it is relied on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CabinetPage>
